comments:
We discussed this failure in the core/infra sync today. I did a brief investigation last week. The assertion that failed is a new one we added because of failures we had seen in 6.8 for this test.

Thankfully the assertion caught a failure case we were missing before (which results in later failures anyways), but unfortunately the exception is incomplete. In particular, the stack frames of the innermost exception are lost in transit, which would tell us what part of HotThreads is reading a negative value and passing that to TimeValue.

@gwbrown Suggested adding assertions before every TimeValue creation in HotThreads, so that when this fails again, we can get a direct culprit, without needing to fix the exception infrastructure (which is sad but that is a much more complex beast to fix).
